WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.169
Our first guest tonight
is an Oscar-nominated,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.471
Emmy, Golden Globe,
and Tony-winning actor

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.173
you know from shows
like "Breaking Bad"

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.675
and "Malcolm in the Middle"
and films like "Trumbo."

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.110
He now stars in "Your Honor."

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.213
The second season finale
premieres March 17th

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.447
on streaming and On Demand

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:18.217
and airs March 19th on Showtime.
Let's take a look.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:22.255
-I held my son in my arms
as he died.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:26.259
♪♪

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.763
-And did you see who shot him?

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.964
-Yes.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.734
-And was it the defendant,
Eugene Jones?

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:41.040
♪♪

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.276
-Yes, it was.
-Please welcome back

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.378
to the show our friend
Bryan Cranston, everybody.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.480
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.480 --> 00:01:02.162
♪♪

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.530
Welcome back!
-Thank you. Good to be back.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.699
It's been four years.
-It's been four years.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.635
I'm very, very happy
to have you here.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.171
-Well, your statute
of limitations was up.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.305
-Yeah.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.307
-And the restraining order
went away.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.509
-And I can't thank you enough
for giving me another chance.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.177
-I -- Well, we'll give it
one more chance.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.745
-And what you are doing
after the show?

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:23.082
-God! Here it goes again, Seth!
Back off!

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.483
-Hey, I wanted to ask.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.886
So, this is a wonderful show
in its second season.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.555
And a very intense show.
You play a --

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.157
-How can you tell?

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.092
-You play a former judge
in new Orleans. This I like.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.760
This poster lets you know
what you're in for.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.395
You're a guy who's
going through some stuff.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:37.830
-He's going through some things,
yeah.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.733
-Obviously this is a real beard.
You did not --

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.501
-That is my real beard, yeah.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.271
-It was a little shorter
in the clip we saw.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.073
So, you trimmed your beard down
over the course of the season.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.943
Did you enjoy walking around
with a big old bush like this?

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.846
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.781
-You see, that's what brought
about the restraining order,

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:57.550
comments like that.
-It's a good word.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.719
It's a good word
for what you're showing me here.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.221
-It is, it is. It's appropriate
and suggestive.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.724
[ Laughter ]
You know, I did because --

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:08.328
It almost created
a mask-like effect.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.463
-Yeah, I would get that.
-And it's nice to be able

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.765
to walk around
and not be so noticed

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.199
and be able to observe,

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:16.469
which is, you know,
part of the actor's tool chest.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.238
-Which gets a little bit harder
to do

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.772
once you become recognizable.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.740
-Now, you've cut it down

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.645
to a very substantive mustache
right now.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.880
-It is --
Yeah, it's a little dip.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.616
I'm doing a movie
with Allison Janney.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.652
It takes place in the '80s.
-Okay.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.755
-And I always think that
someone sets their look

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.958
in the period that they were
really the most formative.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.428
So I think my character might
have set his look in the '70s,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:46.032
with what could be construed
as a porn 'stache.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. I think so.
-Is it? Is it?

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.803
And then so I'm not quite sure.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:55.007
I want to ask your audience
if they think this look

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:57.209
with the little, the little --
What do they call it?

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.311
-Like a soul patch.
-Soul patch here.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:01.880
-Do you think
that looks nastier?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.383
Or does -- Without it?

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:06.285
-Oh, that's
an interesting thing.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:08.687
Alright.
I think with it, it's nastier.

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:09.756
-With it?
-Yeah.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.857
-It's nastier?
-I would say, with it,

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.760
I don't want that guy
to be, like, my pilot.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.762
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.365
-Okay. So I can do this?

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.367
Or else just have my finger here
the whole time.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.569
-Yeah. I think that's
probably the best solution.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.337
-"I see what you mean."

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:27.440
-Because now you're coming off
as a very thoughtful guy.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.575
-"Ahh!"

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.842
-And then you take it away,
though.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.144
You can't take it away,
or it's like,

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.545
"Oh, I've been talking
to a porn actor!"

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.814
[ Laughter ]
"Taking advice from this guy!"

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.415
-That's it.
"What am I doing?!"

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:38.250
What I learned
on "Breaking Bad" --

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.786
Because when I started
that show...

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.919
-I'm glad you brought it up.

00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:42.087
Because we have
some photos here.

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.456
-Oh. There you go.
-'Cause this is great.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.457
I mean, great mustache.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.525
The mustache
to inform the character.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.128
-You can do an entire episode
just on facial hair.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.429
-Yeah.
-I really think you could.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.398
-I would love to. I mean,
would you be my first guest?

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.766
-I will be --
Now, have you --

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.667
Have you worn any --
-I can't do it.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.070
I really -- I've tried.
I would love to grow a mustache.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.906
It would take me from now
until -- I'd be on a deathbed.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:03.075
It just --
It comes in very patchy.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:04.543
-Well, see,
I would love to see that.

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:05.845
-My dad -- You can see it.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.247
Because my dad has a mustache,
and it looks exactly

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.882
-Right.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.984
-Well, when I was doing
"Breaking Bad,"

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.254
I wanted to have my mustache
as Walter White

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.357
before his transition
into Heisenberg.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:20.359
I wanted it to look --

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.295
For lack of a better word,
I said "impotent."

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.263
-Yeah.
-I want an impotent mustache.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.365
-It's a pretty --
It's a pretty impotent mustache.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.767
-Yeah.
-Like, it is weird.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.736
I mean, there's a little
Ned Flanders to it.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.106
-A little Ned Flanders.
"Howdiddy diddily do, neighbor?"

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.840
-Yeah.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.809
-There is a little Ned Flanders
to him, yes.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.079
And what I realized is
there's a few things.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:43.515
You can't have it too dark.
So I lightened it up.

00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:47.152
Also, you can never have
the hair

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.688
curl down below
the crease of the lips.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.791
-Uh-huh.
-If -- Once it -- You can see.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:52.958
-Yeah.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.294
-If I had a mustache
straight across...

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.262
Here I am holding my --
-Do you need a --

00:04:57.262 --> 00:04:59.532
-Yeah. Yeah, there you go.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.203
There you go. See?

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:07.373
You -- You came up with
a three-fingered cover.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.208
-It's like --
-Never grow a mustache

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.610
that needs a three-finger cover!
-Got to have it!

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.179
-And then -- But this is
the transformation.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.148
I mean, look at that.
That is -- I mean --

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.517
It's shocking
that it's the same actor.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.118
I mean, it really is amazing.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.821
And so we wanted to really
make it look different.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:24.390
And so I grew the --
This is actually not --

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.426
If I just had this,
that's a goatee.

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:31.063
But goatee with the mustache
is called a Van Dyke.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:34.166
-Look at you. You're such a --
You're so informed about this.

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.835
But can I tell you --

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.803
can I tell you my favorite
of your mustaches?

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.205
-Yes.
-Cause this is -- this is

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.840
a photo that is beloved
in my home.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.777
-Why?
-Because -- 2014 Emmys.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.545
There was an Emmy party.

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:49.348
And my wife, my sister-in-law,
my brother's girlfriend,

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.184
my cousin,
they took a photo with you.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.020
And I forgot your mustache then.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.088 line:0%
And this was a night where you
brought home a lot of Emmy gold.

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:57.990 line:0%
Look at that one.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.859 line:0%
I mean,
that's a real fun mustache.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.862 line:0%
-It's kind of an Errol Flynn.
-Did you -- Was that for a role?

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.730 line:0%
Or was that just for --

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.100 line:0%
-I was seeing --
I was about to do "Trumbo."

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.135
-There you go.
That's what I thought.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.537
-I was about to do...
and "Trumbo" movie.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.439
And so I wanted to see
if that mustache --

00:06:14.439 --> 00:06:15.841
We ended up not using it.

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:18.344
I think I put
a fake mustache on.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.812
I can't remember.
-Yeah.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.346
-It's too long ago.
-You've had so many mustaches.

00:06:21.346 --> 00:06:24.617
-Lots of mustaches.
I do have fun with facial hair.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.184
-You do.
-I do.

00:06:26.184 --> 00:06:27.586
-And it's fun to watch.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.955
-I have no complaints about
any of the choices you made.

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:32.825
We had your wonderful co-star.
Rosie Perez was here.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.194
And she told about --
She wasn't in season one.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.195
She was in season two
of "Your Honor."

00:06:37.195 --> 00:06:39.998
And you basically --
you called her on a Friday

00:06:39.998 --> 00:06:42.134
for her to come to work
on Monday.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.604
And I would imagine,
you know, with any actor.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:47.239
you have to be pretty convincing
to ask them to get on a plane

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.742
with, you know,
not a lot of time to prepare.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:52.645
-We needed someone formidable,

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:58.184
someone who can -- is known
to have guts and strong.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.853
Right? And her name came up.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.255
I went, "Oh, my God. That's it.
Rosie Perez.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.291
We've got to get Rosie Perez."

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.992
And they said,
"We'll never get her."

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:08.260
She lives in New York.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.596
We're shooting it out in
New Orleans and Los Angeles.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.432
And she has this weekend
to approve,

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:18.504
show up, do a wardrobe test,
and then show up on Monday.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:20.606
And she had scenes with me.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:24.576
My character is going through
some devastating experiences.

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:27.446
And so he's more reticent
on speaking.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.181
So it was all her.

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.717
She had blocks and blocks
of dialogue.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:34.453
And I say things like...
"I don't know."

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.422
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.591
And then blocks and blocks
of dialogue.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:40.793
So I couldn't help her at all,
you know?

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.962
And she was just magnificent.
-Yeah.

00:07:43.962 --> 00:07:46.298
-She just came in
and just crushed it.

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:48.801
-Well, I'm glad
you were that convincing.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.202
I'm glad you got her on board
to do it.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:52.738
-I kind of had to promise,
you know, certain things.

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.339
I'd wash her car.
-Yeah, that's nice.

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:55.774
You're that kind of actor.
-Take the trash out.

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.710
Do whatever.
-You're that kind of guy.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.245
Here's what I'm concerned
and curious --

00:08:00.245 --> 00:08:02.381
is to how you got convinced
to do something.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.650
I have done the wonderful show
"Hot Ones,"

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.418
which I love to watch.
-Oh, yes.

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:07.954
-You also did "Hot Ones."
-Yeah.

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:10.222
-And then you did "Hot Ones"
a second time.

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:12.892
Now, I've known
a lot of people that do it.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.459
I like talking to people
who've done it.

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:17.163
You're the first person
I've heard of who went back in.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.898
Because "Hot Ones" -- This is --

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:20.333
Well, I don't know
if you haven't seen it,

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.768
but you eat chicken wings with
progressively hotter sauces.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.770
It's the most uncomfortable
dining experience

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.304
I've had in my life.

00:08:26.304 --> 00:08:30.543
-It's -- Well -- The answer
to your question, Seth,

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.078
is I have no idea
why I did it a second time.

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:34.880
-Yeah.
-I actually thought --

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.181
Well, the first time I did it,

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:38.884
I was promoting a movie
called "Why Him?"

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:40.719
And I didn't know what it was.

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:42.120
As soon as I was done,

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.723
I thought, "Well,
that'll never last.

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.557
That's a silly premise."
-Yeah.

00:08:45.557 --> 00:08:50.229
But it was -- There's something
intriguing about that show.

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:53.031
And so when they asked me to
come back, I said, "Oh, okay."

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:54.800
And then I thought,
"What am I doing?

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.602
Oh, my God.
I'm doing that hot-sauce show!"

00:08:57.602 --> 00:09:01.240
And there was one hot sauce.
It was in a little jar.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.777
It didn't have as much of
an effect in my mouth

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:07.146
as it did in the chemistry
of my body.

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.881
-Yeah.
-I felt -- You ever have

00:09:09.881 --> 00:09:11.817
one of those moments
where all of a sudden --

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:14.220
"I'm overheating."
I went -- Whoof!

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.922
And my whole head
was starting to sweat.

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:20.159
And I was, like, wip--
It was unbelievable.

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:22.227
I couldn't --
-It is a fascinating --

00:09:22.227 --> 00:09:24.196
I don't -- I mean, you know.
You do it.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:26.365
And you can't --
you stop thinking about

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.234
what's the right or wrong thing
to say.

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:30.302
It's a really novel way
to do an interview

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:32.638
because at some point
I just kept talking

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:35.340
because I thought if I stopped
talking I would die.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.677
-Yes. Yeah.
-And so it's -- I've never seen

00:09:38.677 --> 00:09:41.947
an interview with myself
where I have no memory of it.

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:43.148
-And --
-But that's it.

00:09:43.148 --> 00:09:44.950
-Yeah.
-Do you remember what you said?

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.319
-Almost nothing.
-What secrets did you reveal?

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:50.222
-I think it's too almost
too haunting to watch.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:52.525
People are like,
"You should do ayahuasca."

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:54.393
I'm like, "I think I did it."
-I think --

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.760
-I think
there was maybe a little

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.296
in some of the hot sauces.
-In some of the hot sauce.

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.630
"I'm good."
-Yeah.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.932
Well, I'm very impressed
you did it twice.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.199
Thank you so much for being
here. It's been too long.

00:10:01.199 --> 00:10:04.303
Come back soon. Bryan Cranston.
